       "text": "Nothing in our catalog will give Frank a 12-speed drivetrain on this bike as it stands, so I haven't built a quote or drafted a message.\n\n- **Bike:** it's an 8-speed bike with a Shimano HG 8-10 freehub, a 135 mm QR rear axle and a 26 in wheel. The records show no rear derailleur.\n- **12-speed cassettes:** both need a different freehub body. The 10-44 needs SRAM XD and the 10-36 needs SRAM XDR. Neither fits his HG freehub.\n- **Derailleur:** both 12-speed cassettes also need a matching 12-speed rear derailleur, and none is recorded on the bike.\n- **12-speed chain:** it's rated for 12-speed only, and the drivetrain it would run on doesn't exist yet.\n- **Other cassettes:** the 10-speed and 11-speed cassettes fail on drivetrain speed. The 11-speed road ones also fail on freehub.\n- **Stock:** the 12-speed 10-44 has 1 on the shelf and the 10-36 has none.\n\nA real 12-speed conversion would be a larger project. It would need a rear wheel or freehub body that takes XD or XDR, a 12-speed shifter and derailleur, and likely a new crankset or chainring. It would also need a check that the 1988 steel frame and its 135 mm spacing can take all of that. We have no shifter, derailleur, crank or wheel parts in the system, so I can't quote any of it.\n\nThere are two ways forward:\n- **Source the parts:** you could source the missing 12-speed parts, and I'd then quote them with the labor.\n- **Smaller step:** Frank could stay on 8-speed with a fresh chain and cassette. The catalog has no 8-speed parts that fit, though, so that would also need sourcing.\n\nI can draft Frank a message explaining this and offering those options, if you'd like. I can also open a work order for the conversion assessment.",
